-- **Readout, not sampler.** Every gain of ours comes from reading moments out with a saddlepoint. With accurate moments
-  (2^20 Monte Carlo paths) the median event stays within 50% to 1e-12 at depth 4 and to 1e-6 at depth 8 (1e-8 with the
-  chi mixture). What limits it is the four-term cumulant generating function: tails at depth 8, and far more at depth
-  32 (some outputs reach 1e-12 at 13 SD, others are lighter than Gaussian), depend on higher cumulants that no
-  four-moment readout has.
-- **Backward functions have no leverage at low noise.** At sigma <= 0.01 the event is decided by x through a nonlinear
-  map whose conditional law given the event spreads over many input directions: a Gaussian fitted to it gives 650-3,700
-  relative variance per importance sample, and the noise can carry at most a factor of about 2 (r >= 0.46), so
-  importance sampling and layer-wise twisting over the chain both fail. Splitting needs no psi and handles it with about
-  1e4-1e6 network evaluations per event (1e-4 at depth 4 to 1e-12 at depth 32).
